Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Indices ",
 "2",
 " and ",
 "3",
 " are the contracted bonds; indices ",
 "1",
 " and ",
 "4",
 " are the free legs. The hyperedge lists ",
 "{1,2}",
 ", ",
 "{2,3}",
 ", ",
 "{3,4}",
 " tell the paclet, per tensor, which integer label sits on each leg \[Dash] \
no separate index-naming pass is required. Two natural pair-paths exist for \
this chain: ",
 "{{1,2},{1,2}}",
 " contracts A with B first, then the AB result with C, and ",
 "{{2,3},{1,2}}",
 " contracts B with C first, then with A. For a length-3 chain both cost the \
same; for longer chains the optimal answer is no longer obvious, and that's \
where the planner functions earn their keep. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["PathQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/PathQ"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"201eca10-e94f-43f3-a1db-bacc2c069811"],
 " checks that a list has the right shape \[Dash] every step is a list of one \
or two integers \[Dash] and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CanonicalPathQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/CanonicalPathQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1b1afdd5-6b8c-40b9-94e0-aa05d568615f"],
 " checks the stricter form in which every step is a pair (no unary identity \
steps from a binarization pass):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08440719-3ea5-44f7-89f6-ff68d537a729"],

